msgid "**Cancelling CI runs.** Pull request runs fail fast: the first failed row cancels its siblings in the deploy and workspace matrices, while push and manual runs keep every row. Identical deploy rows from different runs queue behind each other again, keyed on every matrix axis. A cancel now also stops jobs that used to run after a failure: *!cancelled()* replaces *always()*, enforced by lint, and only *done* and *report-main-failures* still report a cancelled run. CodeRabbit reviews draft pull requests too."
