# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized Content Sharing:** Empower users to share photos and visual content across an interoperable, federated network with enhanced privacy controls."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган мазмунду бөлүшүү:** Колдонуучуларга сүрөттөрдү жана визуалдык мазмунду купуялуулукту көзөмөлдөө менен өз ара аракеттенүүчү, федерацияланган тармакта бөлүшүүгө мүмкүнчүлүк берүү."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized Network:** Connect with users across multiple instances in a federated social media ecosystem."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган тармак:** Федерацияланган социалдык медиа экосистемасындагы бир нече инстанциядагы колдонуучулар менен байланышуу."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized Social Networking:** Facilitate a distributed network for seamless peer-to-peer communication."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган социалдык тармактар:** Бир туугандардын ортосундагы үзгүлтүксүз байланыш үчүн бөлүштүрүлгөн тармакты жеңилдетүү."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized Video Hosting:** Distribute video hosting across multiple instances to enhance resilience and avoid single-point control."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган видео хостинг:** Видео хостингди бир нече инстанцияда бөлүштүрүү туруктуулукту жогорулатуу жана бир чекиттик контролдоодон качуу үчүн."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized and Federated:** Connect with a global network of Matrix homeservers, ensuring there is no single point of failure."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган жана федералдык:** Глобалдык тармакка туташуу Matrix Үй кызматчылары, эч кандай кемчилик жок экендигин камсыз кылуу."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Decentralized social networking:** Self-host the AT Protocol PDS and serve user data under your own domain."
msgstr "**Децентралдаштырылган социалдык тармактар:** AT Protocol PDSди өз алдынча кабыл алыңыз жана колдонуучунун маалыматтарын өз домениңизде тейлеңиз."

msgid "**Decided 2026-11-07:** `worldmonitor`, `ais-relay`, `redis-rest` and the seeder are all built from the pinned upstream `v2.11.8` source. The published GHCR image is not used."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision #5, decided by the operator on 2026-11-07:** the implementation builds `worldmonitor`, `ais-relay`, `redis-rest` and the seeder from the pinned `v2.11.8` clone instead of pulling the GHCR image. Evidence at `v2.11.8`: the upstream image publish workflow (`docker-publish`, line 171) builds `ghcr.io/koala73/worldmonitor` from `docker/Dockerfile`, which bakes `VITE_WS_API_URL=https://api.worldmonitor.app` (line 26) and `ENV API_UPSTREAM=https://api.worldmonitor.app` (line 69). That image therefore serves only the frontend and proxies `/api/*` to the upstream cloud, which contradicts the in-stack Redis, seeding and isolation of Decisions #6 to #8. The root `Dockerfile` of the same tag builds the full app with its Node API, and `Dockerfile.relay` and `docker/Dockerfile.redis-rest` build the other two services. Keeping the GHCR image would have needed `API_UPSTREAM` pointed at an in-stack API, which upstream does not ship as a separate image."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision 15, the six consumers.** The decision names WordPress, Moodle, Discourse, OpenProject, Nextcloud and Matrix. An upstream survey of all six found a consumer of a self-hosted LibreTranslate endpoint in two of them:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision 3, the backend gate.** As first written it demanded `lookup('config', '<providing role>', …)` and forbade `group_names`. That gate cannot work: `lookup('config', …)` resolves through `get_merged_applications` ([plugins/lookup/config.py:45](../../plugins/lookup/config.py#L45)), which merges every role in the repository rather than the ones this deploy carries, so `services.ltengine.enabled` reads `true` whether or not LTEngine is deployed and every backend would always be offered. The play-scoped set lives behind a separate lookup ([plugins/lookup/applications_current_play.py:69](../../plugins/lookup/applications_current_play.py#L69)), and the applications cache keys its renders on `group_names` ([utils/cache/base.py:108](../../utils/cache/base.py#L108)) rather than on the whole inventory, so a deployment-wide presence test inside `meta/services.yml` would be cached across inventories that differ."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision 3:** upstream no longer uses Meilisearch; search runs on SQLite FTS inside the aggregator, so no `meilisearch` flag exists."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision 4:** the bridge ships as the `bridge` sidecar of `web-app-atmo`, gated on `web-app-mobilizon` and `web-app-bluesky` in `group_names`, because its source is the platform PDS."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decision 5:** the bridge reconciles against the platform PDS (`listRepos` revisions plus `listRecords`) instead of subscribing to Jetstream. Deletes fall out of the comparison, and a PDS the public relay does not crawl still mirrors."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Declaration driven:** Every proxied repository and every answered hostname comes from the ``cache:`` declarations, collected by the ``cache_upstreams`` and ``cache_repos`` lookups. A new upstream is added by declaring it there."
msgstr "**Декларация:** Ар бир болжолдуу репозиторий жана ар бир жооп берилген хост аты-жөнү ``cache:`` декларацияларды чогултуу ``cache_upstreams`` жана жана ``cache_repos`` издөө. Аны ошол жерде жарыялоо менен жаңы жогору карай кошумчаланат."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Declaration driven:** Every proxied repository and every answered hostname comes from the `cache:` declarations, collected by the `cache_upstreams` and `cache_repos` lookups. A new upstream is added by declaring it there."
msgstr "**Декларация:** Ар бир болжолдуу репозиторий жана ар бир жооп берилген хост аты-жөнү `cache:` декларацияларды чогултуу `cache_upstreams` жана жана `cache_repos` издөө. Аны ошол жерде жарыялоо менен жаңы жогору карай кошумчаланат."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Declared context windows:** A model entry carrying ``context`` publishes it as ``model_info.max_input_tokens``, and an Ollama entry also runs with that window as ``num_ctx`` instead of the server’s default, so a caller’s prompt is not silently truncated."
msgstr "**Декларацияланган контексттик терезелер:** Моделдик кирүү ``context`` аны жарыялайт ``model_info.max_input_tokens``, жана Ollama кирүү ошондой эле терезе менен жүрөт ``num_ctx`` Сервердин демейки мөөнөтүнүн ордуна, чалуучунун чакырыгы үнсүз кыскартылбайт."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Declared context windows:** A model entry carrying `context` publishes it as `model_info.max_input_tokens`, and an Ollama entry also runs with that window as `num_ctx` instead of the server's default, so a caller's prompt is not silently truncated."
msgstr "**Декларацияланган контексттик терезелер:** Моделдик кирүү `context` аны жарыялайт `model_info.max_input_tokens`, жана Ollama кирүү ошондой эле терезе менен жүрөт `num_ctx` Сервердин демейки мөөнөтүнүн ордуна, чалуучунун чакырыгы үнсүз кыскартылбайт."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Declared hardware access:** Every device the agent may drive is listed by the operator and bound into the container; an empty list is refused rather than silently treated as deny-all-but-deployable."
msgstr "**Декларацияланган аппараттык кирүү:** Агент айдай турган ар бир шайман оператор тарабынан тизмеге киргизилип, контейнерге байланат; бош тизме унчукпай эле жокко чыгарылат, бирок жокко чыгарылат."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Declared per application, literally.** Every consumer role declares `stack: {enabled: true, shared: true}` in its own `meta/services.yml`. The values are fixed literals, not `'<role>' in group_names` expressions. A central per-category declaration and the `add_host` injection used for OpenResty were rejected."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decommission:** On a compose deploy without `--id` and with `CLEANUP`, the destructor stops every compose instance directly below `DIR_COMPOSITIONS` that no active role owns with `compose down --remove-orphans` and then deletes it, before `sys-service-terminator` starts the deferred services and the CLI tests run. The instance's named volumes stay; bind-mounted data inside the directory, such as `volumes/`, goes with it. A role counts as active when any host of the inventory carries it, when it is in the `CURRENT_PLAY_APPLICATIONS` dependency closure, or when the play prepared its instance. Only a directory named after a known role and carrying the full instance layout (`compose.yml`, `.env/`, `config/`, `services/`, `volumes/`) counts as an instance. An instance that a container outside its compose project is named after, such as a launcher-managed container, stays too. Every directory left alone is listed in the deploy output. The deploy fails before deleting anything when a container still carries the stopped project's name or working directory. A failure of the decommission, the deferred services or the CLI tests still unlocks the timers and fails the deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Decommission:** On a compose deploy without ``--id`` and with ``CLEANUP``, the destructor stops every compose instance directly below ``DIR_COMPOSITIONS`` that no active role owns with ``compose down --remove-orphans`` and then deletes it, before ``sys-service-terminator`` starts the deferred services and the CLI tests run. The instance’s named volumes stay; bind-mounted data inside the directory, such as ``volumes/``, goes with it. A role counts as active when any host of the inventory carries it, when it is in the ``CURRENT_PLAY_APPLICATIONS`` dependency closure, or when the play prepared its instance. Only a directory named after a known role and carrying the full instance layout (``compose.yml``, ``.env/``, ``config/``, ``services/``, ``volumes/``) counts as an instance. An instance that a container outside its compose project is named after, such as a launcher-managed container, stays too. Every directory left alone is listed in the deploy output. The deploy fails before deleting anything when a container still carries the stopped project’s name or working directory. A failure of the decommission, the deferred services or the CLI tests still unlocks the timers and fails the deploy."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Dedicated device only.** Full access is permitted solely on a node whose only tenant is this agent. Forbidden on any shared cluster node (Decision #12)."
msgstr "**Атайын шайман гана.** Толук кирүүгө бул агент жалгыз ижарачысы болгон түйүндө гана уруксат берилет. Ар бир бөлүшүлгөн кластердик түйүнгө тыюу салынат (Чечим #12)...."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Dedicated domain:** The admin UI is reachable on its own canonical hostname under the primary domain."
msgstr "**Атайын домен:** Админдик UI негизги домендин астында өзүнүн канондук хост аталышы менен жеткиликтүү."

msgid "**Dedicated runner:** Templates never run inside the server container: the server sets `SEMAPHORE_USE_REMOTE_RUNNER=true` and hands every task to the `task-runner` service, which signs in with the runner token the deploy seeds. Its image is an Infinito.Nexus image (`SOFTWARE_IMAGE`) plus the `semaphore` binary of the pinned server image, tagged with the tag of that Infinito.Nexus image. It mounts no Docker socket, runs as an unprivileged user, and reaches hosts only over SSH with the key held in the key store of the project."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Dedicated runner:** Templates never run inside the server container: the server sets ``SEMAPHORE_USE_REMOTE_RUNNER=true`` and hands every task to the ``task-runner`` service, which signs in with the runner token the deploy seeds. Its image is an Infinito.Nexus image (``SOFTWARE_IMAGE``) plus the ``semaphore`` binary of the pinned server image, tagged with the tag of that Infinito.Nexus image. It mounts no Docker socket, runs as an unprivileged user, and reaches hosts only over SSH with the key held in the key store of the project."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Dedicated, single-tenant, segmented node only.** The role MUST refuse to deploy on a node that carries any shared-workload label or hosts other tenants, and the node MUST be network-segmented from shared infrastructure. This is enforced, not just documented: a placement/preflight guard hard-fails on a shared node."
msgstr "**Атайын, бир ижарачы, сегменттелген түйүн гана.** Бул ролду бөлүшүү жүктү белгилөө же башка ижарачыларды жайгаштыруу түйүнүнө жайгаштыруудан баш тартуу керек жана түйүн бөлүшүлгөн инфраструктурадан тармактык сегменттештирилиши керек. Бул жөн гана документтештирилген эмес: жалпы түйүндөгү жайгаштыруу же учуу алдындагы күзөт катуу кемчиликтери."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Dedicated-device guard:** Deployment aborts when another application shares the host or when the device is part of a multi-node swarm, naming the offender."
msgstr "**Жабдуунун атайын коргоочусу:** Башка тиркеме хостту бөлүшкөндө же шайман көп түйүндүү үйүрдүн бир бөлүгү болгондо, кылмышкердин атын атаганда, жайгаштыруу токтотулат."

