msgid "**Test notes.** The RBAC tiers are proven by moving `biber` through the groups with LAM's Multi edit tool and asserting both the grant and the revoke, rather than by dedicated accounts. `/ui/vault/logout` does not end a session — the Ember app restores its token from browser storage — so use the UI's own logout control when the session must actually be gone."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Test variant:** Variant 0 of [meta/variants.yml](./meta/variants.yml) deploys `web-app-gitea` next to Semaphore and declares the block with the private repository `target-inventory` of the platform administrator on the SSH port of that Gitea, the branch `main`, the `deploy_ssh_key` credential as repository key and a fixed vault password. On the `dev`, `act` and `github` runtimes, with Gitea and the block present, [tasks/utils/project/fixture.yml](./tasks/utils/project/fixture.yml) runs before the projects converge: it reads the address, pinned host keys and public root key of the [shared target](../../compose/target/README.md) from the holder, authorizes the deploy key for `root` on the target, recreates the repository whenever its `.infinito-fixture` marker no longer matches the repository key, vault password, host, application and variables, with an inventory for the host `target` that includes `web-svc-html` under `TLS_MODE` `self_signed` and the `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` of the stack, and binds the public half of the repository key to the repository as a read-only deploy key. The `deploy` environment then pins the host keys of the target. [test-foreign-deploy.js](./files/playwright/test-foreign-deploy.js) signs in as `administrator` through Keycloak, requires that port 443 of the target still refuses, runs `deploy`, waits up to 60 minutes for the task, and opens `https://html.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/` in a browser that resolves that name to the target. It runs in the first pass only, the pass the target is reset for."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Test variant:** Variant 0 of `meta/variants.yml <./meta/variants.yml>`__ deploys ``web-app-gitea`` next to Semaphore and declares the block with the private repository ``target-inventory`` of the platform administrator on the SSH port of that Gitea, the branch ``main``, the ``deploy_ssh_key`` credential as repository key and a fixed vault password. On the ``dev``, ``act`` and ``github`` runtimes, with Gitea and the block present, `tasks/utils/project/fixture.yml <./tasks/utils/project/fixture.yml>`__ runs before the projects converge: it reads the address, pinned host keys and public root key of the `shared target <../../compose/target/README.md>`__ from the holder, authorizes the deploy key for ``root`` on the target, recreates the repository whenever its ``.infinito-fixture`` marker no longer matches the repository key, vault password, host, application and variables, with an inventory for the host ``target`` that includes ``web-svc-html`` under ``TLS_MODE`` ``self_signed`` and the ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY`` of the stack, and binds the public half of the repository key to the repository as a read-only deploy key. The ``deploy`` environment then pins the host keys of the target. `test-foreign-deploy.js <./files/playwright/test-foreign-deploy.js>`__ signs in as ``administrator`` through Keycloak, requires that port 443 of the target still refuses, runs ``deploy``, waits up to 60 minutes for the task, and opens ``https://html.<DOMAIN_PRIMARY>/`` in a browser that resolves that name to the target. It runs in the first pass only, the pass the target is reset for."
msgstr ""

