# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The scope of this folder is waiting and availability checks. Build, release, and resource-specific lifecycle operations should stay in their dedicated directories."
msgstr "Бул папканын чөйрөсү күтүү жана жеткиликтүүлүк текшерүүлөрү болуп саналат. Курулуш, бошотуу жана ресурстарга тиешелүү жашоо циклинин операциялары алардын атайын каталогдорунда сакталышы керек."

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The script MUST act on the container through `container exec \"${GARBAGE_COLLECTOR_ADDRESS}\"`, using the application's native commands where they exist. Raw deletes are reserved for files the application cannot clean itself. It MUST NOT use host volume paths: a volume MAY be NFS or sit on another node."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script MUST be idempotent."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script MUST take exactly one argument, the mode: `routine` (daily timer) or `pressure` (the disc space cleaner found a full disk)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script first starts the role's deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (`rsync -aHAX --delete`): `secrets` into `/var/lib/infinito/secrets`, `ca` into `/etc/<domain>/ca`, `acme` into `/etc/letsencrypt`, `certbot` into `/etc/certbot`. `--no-safety-backup` skips the pre-recover unit run. The `node` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with `--restore-node-identity`, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host's identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script first starts the role’s deployed backup unit (a fresh differential generation of the live material), then mirrors each present subtree back to its fixed system path (``rsync -aHAX --delete``): ``secrets`` into ``/var/lib/infinito/secrets``, ``ca`` into ``/etc/<domain>/ca``, ``acme`` into ``/etc/letsencrypt``, ``certbot`` into ``/etc/certbot``. ``--no-safety-backup`` skips the pre-recover unit run. The ``node`` subtree (ssh host keys + machine-id) is restored only with ``--restore-node-identity``, because overwriting the running machine-id / ssh host keys changes the host’s identity mid-flight — do it on a fresh host after total loss."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script formats a disk only when all of these hold; otherwise the runner stays as it is:"
msgstr ""

# Композиция жана үйүр жолдорду ар кандай жолдор менен акчаны жууйт (а а а
# ``$pid`` контейнерге жеткенде ``""`` "Анын ордуна, ""Sh"" синтаксис катасы
# менен капталдагы арабаны байлап койду."). Ошондуктан чакалуу кабиналар
# сурамжылоолорго катышат ``/status`` фондук суб-кабыктан ``exec`` Сервердин
# PID 1• сурамжылоо цикли контейнер менен өлөт жана даярдык керектөөчүнүн
# чектелген күтүүсү менен чектелет.
msgid "The script must stay free of every shell ``$``: the compose and swarm render paths launder dollars differently (a ``$pid`` reached the container as ``\"\"`` and crash-looped the sidecar on a sh syntax error). The bucket bootstrap therefore polls ``/status`` from a backgrounded subshell while ``exec`` makes the server PID 1; the poll loop dies with the container and readiness is gated by the consumer's bounded wait."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script of a letter, not its codepoint range: ``ð`` and ``í`` are Latin and not ASCII, which is the difference between reading pseudo-Faroese as Latin text and reading it as something else."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; `--passphrase-stdin` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (`rsync -aHAX --delete`) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role's `recover.py` (`svc-bkp-volume-2-local` for docker volumes, `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local` for NFS exports)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script opens the LUKS device (interactive passphrase prompt; ``--passphrase-stdin`` for automation), mounts it, picks the newest device snapshot across every machine hash (a fresh host after total loss has a new machine id), mirrors it into the target (``rsync -aHAX --delete``) and unmounts/closes the device again. No pre-recover service backup runs: the device itself is the backup this role maintains. Afterwards restore individual applications from the backup root with the matching role’s ``recover.py`` (``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` for docker volumes, ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` for NFS exports)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The script puts the swapfile on `/` when containerd already lives on `/mnt`, **prefers `/mnt`** otherwise when it is a separate partition (classic `ubuntu-latest` layout with `/dev/sdb` mounted at `/mnt`), and falls back to `/`. Current public runners no longer expose a separate `/mnt`, so the swapfile lands on `/` and must not starve the root filesystem."
msgstr ""

