msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixelfed’s login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed’s first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. ``biber`` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed’s ``dns,spoof`` validator rejects ``.example`` addresses. Both setups live in `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ and drive the dedicated login specs in ``files/playwright/``."
msgstr "Бөлүнгөн ``biber`` жана жана ``administrator`` жекече жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Pixelfed's login id - бул электрондук почта эмес, электрондук почта. Keycloak Колдонуучунун аты жана кол өнөрчүлүк менен бекемделген администратордун аты сакталып калган, ошондуктан пикселфеддин биринчи жолу OIDC каттоосу да аны бөлүп чыгара албайт. ``biber`` кошумча анын муктаждыктары Keycloak Электрондук почта аркылуу жөнгө салынуучу доменге кайра жазылган Keycloak admin API Биринчи OIDC кирүүдөн мурун, анткени пикселфед ``dns,spoof`` валидациялоочу четке кагат ``.example`` даректер. Эки түзүлүш тең тирүү `files/playwright/\\_shared.js <./files/playwright/_shared.js>`__ Бул атайын кирүү спектрин камтыйт. ``files/playwright/``...."

# жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат
# `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. OpenTalk
# Frontend - бул коомдук кардар OIDC бир барактан турган тиркемеси <unk>
# контейнердик env эмитент жана клиенттик идентификатордон башка эч нерсе алып
# жүрбөйт, сервер тараптагы сессия жана HTML кирүү формасы жок <unk>
# ошондуктан рол аны өзүнүн багыттоочу жарыш жардамчысы менен башкарат.
# ``LOGIN_*`` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / ``BIBER_*`` ордуна ``ADMIN_*`` Бөлүнгөн жардамчы
# күтөт, ал эми браузер тараптагы сессия келишимдин колдонмодогу кирүү
# баскычын максатсыз калтырат. Эки инсан тең Keycloak Dashboard чынжырчасы
# `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js
# <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__....
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The OpenTalk frontend is a public-client OIDC single-page app — the container env carries nothing but the issuer and the client id, there is no server-side session and no HTML login form — so the role drives it with its own redirect-racing helper keyed on ``LOGIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` instead of the ``ADMIN_*`` pair the shared helper expects, and the browser-side session leaves the contract’s in-app logout leg without a target. Both personas’ Keycloak → dashboard chain is covered by `files/playwright/test-sso-login.js <./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js>`__."
msgstr ""

# жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат
# `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. Роль
# жоболору эч кандай алдын ала эсепке алынбайт <unk> `tasks/main.yml
# <./tasks/main.yml>`__ Pretixтин жергиликтүү auth арткы бөлүгү pretixти
# аутентификациялайт ``User`` Бул интерактивдүү биринчи чуркоо орнотуусу менен
# түзүлгөн сап. " ``pretix-oidc`` Претикс боюнча жогорку өмүргө кошумчаланган
# арткы чекит ``/control`` Бул жерде, ал эми ролдордун базалык URL коомдук
# билет дүкөнүнө кызмат кылат, ал эми базалык сценарийлер
# `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js
# <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ ырастоо. Арткы колдонуучуну себүү
# - бул чуркоочу инсандык саякатка кайтып келүү жолу.
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona helpers are declared blocked in `templates/playwright.env.j2 <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__. The role provisions no pretix account at all — `tasks/main.yml <./tasks/main.yml>`__ only deploys the stack — while pretix’s native auth backend authenticates a pretix ``User`` row that is created by the interactive first-run setup. The ``pretix-oidc`` backend added on top lives on pretix’s ``/control`` login page, whereas the role’s base URL serves the public ticket shop that the baseline scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ assert. Seeding a backend user is the path back to a runnable persona journey."
msgstr ""

# саякаттар ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` ичинде ``templates/playwright.env.j2``.
# Fider's SSO жазуусу эки баскычтуу модал: баштык <unk>Sign in<unk> баскычы
# провайдердин диалогун гана ачат жана <unk>SSO менен улантуу<unk> экинчи
# чыкылдатуу <unk>SSO менен улантуу<unk> Keycloak Башка жакка багыттоо, ал эми
# бөлүшүлгөн жардамчы так бир жолу чыкылдатып, эч качан IdPге жетпейт. Эки
# саякат тең ушул ролдун өзүнөн-өзү аяктайт ``fider: admin sso login`` жана
# жана ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` сценарийлер
# ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``• бөлүшүлгөн жардамчы үйрөнгөндөн
# кийин, opt-out мөөнөтү аяктайт FiderМодалдык.
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Fider’s SSO entry is a two-step modal: the header “Sign in” button only opens the provider dialog, and a second click on “Continue with … SSO” performs the Keycloak redirect, whereas the shared helper clicks exactly once and never reaches the IdP. Both journeys are covered end-to-end by this role’s own ``fider: admin sso login`` and ``fider: biber sso login as regular user`` scenarios in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``; the opt-out lapses once the shared helper learns Fider’s modal."
msgstr ""

# саякаттар ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` ичинде ``templates/playwright.env.j2``.
# OIDC вариантынан тышкары, ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` тандап алат ``ldap`` же
# же ``local`` коопсуздук чөйрөсү жана Jenkins<unk> бир гана кирүү бети өзүнчө
# Java- реалдуу форма, анын талаалары аталган ``j_username`` / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# ``j_password`` (LDAP сценарийинин негизинде
# ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) <unk> жалпы жергиликтүү логин
# зонддорунун аталыштары дал келбейт, ошондуктан инсан эч качан
# аутентификациялабайт. Учурда желек эч кандай шартсыз; аны таркатуу ``{% if
# not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` OIDC инсандык саякаты текшерилгенден кийин,
# артка кайтуу жолу болот.
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. Outside the OIDC variant, ``templates/casc.yaml.j2`` selects the ``ldap`` or ``local`` security realm and Jenkins’ only login surface is its own Java-realm form, whose fields are named ``j_username`` / ``j_password`` (pinned by the LDAP scenario in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``) — names the shared native-login probe does not match, so the persona never authenticates. The flag is currently unconditional; narrowing it to ``{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}`` once the OIDC persona journey has been verified end-to-end is the path back."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. The site front page renders no logout control: Joomla’s site template places no login module, and the only rendered Log out button sits on the com_users login view, so the persona’s mandatory in-app logout click on the front page has no target and navigating a logout URL directly is forbidden by the contract. The OIDC handshake itself, the Keycloak logout from the com_users Log out button, the LDAP variant and the ``/administrator?fallback=local`` hatch are covered by ``files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js``, ``test-sso-logout.js``, ``test-ldap-login.js`` and ``test-oidc-fallback.js``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. ``biber`` holds no FusionDirectory role, so the oauth2-proxy denies it. ```files/playwright/test-rbac.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac.js>`__ asserts that denial and adds ``biber`` to each role group in turn to assert the rights of the matching ACL role. The shared admin flow has not been verified against the header login. ```files/playwright/test-design.js`` <./files/playwright/test-design.js>`__ asserts the administrator’s sign-in and rights in both variants, and ```files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` <./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js>`__ asserts that the Keycloak sign-in lands in FusionDirectory without a second login form."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` and ``administrator`` persona journeys are opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. web-app-hugo serves a statically built site: ``services.sso`` is hard-disabled in ``meta/services.yml``, the container is a Hugo build baked into nginx (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), and the Playwright env file renders no ``ADMIN_*`` / ``BIBER_*`` credentials. There is no session, no admin surface and no logout control to drive, so the ``guest`` persona plus the reachability, CSP and rendered-HTML assertions are the complete contract for this role."
msgstr "Бөлүнгөн ``biber`` жана жана ``administrator`` Жеке саякаттар ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED`` ичинде ``templates/playwright.env.j2``.... web-app-hugo Статикалык курулган жерди тейлейт: ``services.sso`` катуу майып ``meta/services.yml``, контейнер - бул Hugo Нинкске бышырылган (``templates/compose.yml.j2``), Playwright Env файлы ``ADMIN_*`` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / ``BIBER_*`` күбөлүктөр. Бул жерде эч кандай сеанс жок, эч кандай администратордук бети жок жана эч кандай башкаруу жок, ошондуктан айдоо үчүн, ``guest`` Бул рол үчүн толук келишим болуп саналат."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared ``biber`` persona journey is opted out via ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` in ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. A Jellyfin account binds to exactly one authentication provider, so biber’s login is owned by the per-addon specs that know which provider is live: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` for OIDC and ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` for the LDAP-only matrix variant. The generic persona cannot pick between them and would duplicate or contradict that coverage; ``playwright.spec.js`` keeps the ``guest`` scenario and the native administrator login."
msgstr "Бөлүнгөн ``biber`` жекече саякат ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED`` ичинде ``templates/playwright.env.j2``. А. Jellyfin Аккаунт так бир аутентификация берүүчүгө байланат, ошондуктан биобердин кирүүсү кайсы провайдер тирүү экенин билген бир аддонго таандык: ``files/playwright/addons/sso-authentication.spec.js`` OIDC үчүн ``addons/ldap-authentication.spec.js`` LDAP матрицасынын варианты Жалпы персонал алардын арасынан тандай албайт жана бул камтууну кайталайт же карама-каршы келет; ``playwright.spec.js`` сактоо ``guest`` Сценарий жана жергиликтүү администратордун кирүүсү."

msgid "The shared `administrator` persona journey is opted out via `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Flowise has no in-app OIDC adapter: SSO is an oauth2-proxy sidecar (`services.sso.flavor: oauth2`), and behind that gate Flowise still presents its own sign-in form for its single instance account `flowise-api-bot`, which `tasks/utils/owner.yml` registers. The Keycloak administrator credential the persona types is not that account's, so the journey cannot reach an authenticated Flowise surface; the OIDC gate itself is covered by `files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js`."
msgstr ""

# жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud
# вариантына жараша үч башка кирүү бетин көрсөтөт (жергиликтүү, `oidc_login`,
# `sociallogin`)Жергиликтүү администратор жергиликтүү ролдук администратор
# менен аутентификациялайт `credentials.administrator_password` тескерисинче
# Keycloak жашыруун жана `#firstrunwizard` Модалдык тосуп алуу колдонуучунун
# менюсун чыкылдатып, жалпы кирүү көз каранды. Демек, эки инсан тең ролдун
# өзүлөрүнүн кирүү өзгөчөлүктөрү менен башкарылат <unk>
# `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`,
# `test-login-biber-oidc.js` жана жана `test-login-biber-ldap.js` астында
# астында `files/playwright/` <unk> даамын өчүргүчтү, модалдык четке кагууну
# жана бөлүшүлгөн жардамчынын жетишсиздигин алып жүрүүчү.
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Nextcloud presents three different login surfaces depending on the variant (native, `oidc_login`, `sociallogin`), the native administrator authenticates with the role-local `credentials.administrator_password` rather than the Keycloak secret, and the `#firstrunwizard` modal intercepts the user-menu click the generic logout depends on. Both personas are therefore driven by the role's own login specs — `test-login-admin-native.js`, `test-login-admin-oidc.js`, `test-login-biber-oidc.js` and `test-login-biber-ldap.js` under `files/playwright/` — which carry the flavor switch, the modal dismissal and the login retry the shared helper lacks."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Odoo renders its SSO provider link only on `/web/login` inside the `.o_login_auth` container, not on the site root the persona helper starts from, and it exposes no in-app logout control — signing out means navigating to `/web/session/logout`. The full Keycloak round trip for both users is covered by the role's own `odoo: admin sso login, verify ui, logout` and `odoo: biber sso login, verify ui, logout` scenarios in [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js); the second joins `biber` to the `user` role group first, because a Keycloak user without an Odoo role is refused. [files/playwright/test-rbac.js](./files/playwright/test-rbac.js) covers every role and the profile mapping."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenCloud Web answers Playwright's headless Chromium user agent with a \"browser not supported\" splash unless `forceAllowOldBrowser` is seeded into `localStorage` before the first navigation, and its OIDC callback runs through OpenCloud's own `/oidc-callback` → `/web-oidc-callback` routes instead of the oauth2-proxy pattern the shared helper detects. Both personas' Keycloak round trip is covered by [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js), which does that priming in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixelfed's login id is the account e-mail rather than the Keycloak username, and the artisan-bootstrapped administrator name is reserved, so pixelfed's first-time OIDC registration cannot mint it either. `biber` additionally needs his Keycloak e-mail rewritten to a resolvable domain through the Keycloak admin API before the first OIDC login, because pixelfed's `dns,spoof` validator rejects `.example` addresses. Both setups live in [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) and drive the dedicated login specs in `files/playwright/`."
msgstr "Бөлүнгөн `biber` жана жана `administrator` жекече жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Pixelfed's login id - бул электрондук почта эмес, электрондук почта. Keycloak Колдонуучунун аты-жөнү жана кол өнөрчүлүк менен бекемделген администратордун аты-жөнү сакталып калган, ошондуктан пиксельфеддин биринчи жолу OIDC каттоосу да аны тазалай албайт. `biber` кошумча анын муктаждыктары Keycloak Электрондук почта аркылуу жөнгө салынуучу доменге кайра жазылган Keycloak admin API Биринчи OIDC кирүүдөн мурун, пикселфед `dns,spoof` валидациялоочу четке кагат `.example` даректер. Эки түзүлүш тең тирүү [files/playwright/_shared.js](./files/playwright/_shared.js) Бул атайын кирүү спектрин камтыйт. `files/playwright/`...."

# жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). OpenTalk
# Frontend - бул коомдук кардар OIDC бир барактан турган тиркемеси <unk>
# контейнердик env эмитент жана клиенттик идентификатордон башка эч нерсе алып
# жүрбөйт, сервер тараптагы сессия жана HTML кирүү формасы жок <unk>
# ошондуктан рол аны өзүнүн багыттоочу жарыш жардамчысы менен башкарат.
# `LOGIN_*` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / `BIBER_*` ордуна `ADMIN_*` Биргелешкен жардамчы
# күтөт, ал эми браузер тараптагы сессия келишимдин колдонмодогу кирүү
# баскычын максатсыз калтырат. Эки инсан тең Keycloak Dashboard чынжырчасы
# [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js)....
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). The OpenTalk frontend is a public-client OIDC single-page app — the container env carries nothing but the issuer and the client id, there is no server-side session and no HTML login form — so the role drives it with its own redirect-racing helper keyed on `LOGIN_*` / `BIBER_*` instead of the `ADMIN_*` pair the shared helper expects, and the browser-side session leaves the contract's in-app logout leg without a target. Both personas' Keycloak → dashboard chain is covered by [files/playwright/test-sso-login.js](./files/playwright/test-sso-login.js)."
msgstr ""

# жардам берүүчүлөр тоскоолдукка учураган деп жарыяланат
# [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). Роль жоболору
# эч кандай алдын ала эсепке алынбайт <unk> [tasks/main.yml](./tasks/main.yml)
# Pretixтин жергиликтүү auth арткы бөлүгү pretixти аутентификациялайт `User`
# Бул интерактивдүү биринчи чуркоо орнотуусу менен түзүлгөн сап. "
# `pretix-oidc` Претикс менен жогорку жашоонун кошумчалары `/control` Бул
# жерде, ал эми URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL
# URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL URL
# URL URL URL URL
# [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js)
# ырастоо. Арткы колдонуучуну себүү - бул чуркоочу инсандык саякатка кайтып
# келүү жолу.
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona helpers are declared blocked in [templates/playwright.env.j2](./templates/playwright.env.j2). The role provisions no pretix account at all — [tasks/main.yml](./tasks/main.yml) only deploys the stack — while pretix's native auth backend authenticates a pretix `User` row that is created by the interactive first-run setup. The `pretix-oidc` backend added on top lives on pretix's `/control` login page, whereas the role's base URL serves the public ticket shop that the baseline scenarios in [files/playwright/playwright.spec.js](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js) assert. Seeding a backend user is the path back to a runnable persona journey."
msgstr ""

# саякаттар `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` ичинде `templates/playwright.env.j2`.
# Fider's SSO жазуусу эки баскычтуу модал: баштык "Белги" баскыч провайдердин
# диалогун гана ачат, жана экинчи чыкылдатуу "SSO менен улантуу..." аткаруучу
# Keycloak Башка жакка багыттоо, ал эми бөлүшүлгөн жардамчы так бир жолу
# чыкылдатып, эч качан IdPге жетпейт. Эки саякат тең ушул ролдун өзү тарабынан
# аягына чейин камтылган `fider: admin sso login` жана жана `fider: biber sso
# login as regular user` сценарийлер `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`•
# бөлүшүлгөн жардамчы үйрөнгөндөн кийин, opt-out мөөнөтү аяктайт Fider"s
# modal.
# gained=['"Белги"']
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Fider's SSO entry is a two-step modal: the header \"Sign in\" button only opens the provider dialog, and a second click on \"Continue with … SSO\" performs the Keycloak redirect, whereas the shared helper clicks exactly once and never reaches the IdP. Both journeys are covered end-to-end by this role's own `fider: admin sso login` and `fider: biber sso login as regular user` scenarios in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`; the opt-out lapses once the shared helper learns Fider's modal."
msgstr ""

# саякаттар `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` ичинде `templates/playwright.env.j2`. OIDC
# вариантынан тышкары, `templates/casc.yaml.j2` тандап алат `ldap` же же
# `local` коопсуздук чөйрөсү жана Jenkins"Жөн гана кирүү бети өзүнчө Java-
# реалдуу форма, анын талаалары аталган `j_username` / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / / /
# `j_password` (LDAP сценарийинин негизинде
# `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`) <unk> жалпы жергиликтүү логин
# зонддорунун аталыштары дал келбейт, ошондуктан инсан эч качан
# аутентификациялабайт. Учурда желек эч кандай шартсыз; аны таркатуу `{% if
# not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}` OIDC инсандык саякаты текшерилгенден кийин,
# артка кайтуу жолу болот.
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. Outside the OIDC variant, `templates/casc.yaml.j2` selects the `ldap` or `local` security realm and Jenkins' only login surface is its own Java-realm form, whose fields are named `j_username` / `j_password` (pinned by the LDAP scenario in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`) — names the shared native-login probe does not match, so the persona never authenticates. The flag is currently unconditional; narrowing it to `{% if not JENKINS_OIDC_ENABLED %}` once the OIDC persona journey has been verified end-to-end is the path back."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. The site front page renders no logout control: Joomla's site template places no login module, and the only rendered Log out button sits on the com_users login view, so the persona's mandatory in-app logout click on the front page has no target and navigating a logout URL directly is forbidden by the contract. The OIDC handshake itself, the Keycloak logout from the com_users Log out button, the LDAP variant and the `/administrator?fallback=local` hatch are covered by `files/playwright/test-oidc-login.js`, `test-sso-logout.js`, `test-ldap-login.js` and `test-oidc-fallback.js`."
msgstr ""

msgid "The shared `biber` and `administrator` persona journeys are opted out via `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED` / `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. `biber` holds no FusionDirectory role, so the oauth2-proxy denies it. [`files/playwright/test-rbac.js`](./files/playwright/test-rbac.js) asserts that denial and adds `biber` to each role group in turn to assert the rights of the matching ACL role. The shared admin flow has not been verified against the header login. [`files/playwright/test-design.js`](./files/playwright/test-design.js) asserts the administrator's sign-in and rights in both variants, and [`files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`](./files/playwright/playwright.spec.js) asserts that the Keycloak sign-in lands in FusionDirectory without a second login form."
msgstr ""

