msgid "[ ] No application receives an unverified address in the `email` claim. Static half (operator decision 2026-11-07: realm `verifyEmail: true` plus `trustEmail: true` on the LDAP federation): with SMTP the realm import sets `verifyEmail` (`KEYCLOAK_EMAIL_VERIFY` in `roles/web-app-keycloak/vars/main.yml`) and every deploy converges it onto an existing realm through `KEYCLOAK_SETTINGS_SPEC`; the federation sets `trustEmail: true` in `roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/import/components/org.keycloak.storage.UserStorageProvider.json.j2`, which the LDAP component merge carries onto existing realms. Upstream Keycloak 26.8.2 then adds `VERIFY_EMAIL` to every user with an unverified, non-blank address (`services/.../authentication/requiredactions/VerifyEmail.java:76-89`), refuses a password grant while a required action is pending (`services/.../protocol/oidc/grants/ResourceOwnerPasswordCredentialsGrantType.java:125-138`), and marks a user verified when the federation first imports it (`federation/ldap/.../LDAPStorageProvider.java:695-697`, called only for new users at `:753` and from the sync at `LDAPStorageProviderFactory.java:771-774`). A client credentials grant evaluates no required action (`ClientCredentialsGrantType.java:87-133`), so service accounts are not held. Directory users imported before `trustEmail` turned on get the same trust from `email_verified.py` with `FEDERATION` (`roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/update/06_users/email_federated.yml`), which runs before the settings converge turns `verifyEmail` on and never touches a user without the LDAP `federationLink` (`TestFederation` and `TestDirectoryTrustOrder` in `tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-keycloak/files/test_email_verified.py`). Deploy-created realm users get `emailVerified: true` from `roles/web-app-keycloak/files/python/email_verified.py` while `services.keycloak.users.emails_verified` is on. Mailbox mode emits the mailbox with a hardcoded `email_verified: true` and keeps `verifyEmail: false`. Proven by `test_with_mail_no_unverified_address_reaches_the_email_claim`, `test_the_federation_trusts_the_directory_addresses_in_every_policy`, `test_an_untrusted_federation_fails_the_check` and `test_without_mail_the_realm_cannot_demand_a_verification` in `tests/unit/python/roles/web-app-keycloak/templates/test_realm_import_json.py`, and `test_an_existing_realm_converges_to_the_verify_email_flag_of_the_dictionary` in `tests/unit/python/roles/web_app_keycloak/test_saml_clients_on_existing_realms.py`. Open: without SMTP `verifyEmail` stays off, so an address an administrator left unverified still reaches the claim with `email_verified: false`; a session or offline token issued before the flag turned on keeps its claim until it ends, since a refresh evaluates no required action; an address changed in LDAP outside Keycloak keeps the user's flag."
msgstr ""

